; /var/lib/knot/acme.example.com.zone
; Initial zone file. After the first load Knot keeps changes in its journal
; and this file is no longer rewritten (zonefile-sync: -1).
;
; REPLACE:
;   acme.example.com        -> your delegated zone
;   ns-certpull.example.com -> the NS name pointing at this server
;   pki@example.com         -> contact address (@ becomes .)

$ORIGIN acme.example.com.
$TTL 300

@   IN  SOA ns-certpull.example.com. pki.example.com. (
            2026010101  ; serial
            3600        ; refresh
            600         ; retry
            604800      ; expire
            60 )        ; minimum = negative TTL (short, so a cached NXDOMAIN hurts less)

@   IN  NS  ns-certpull.example.com.

; Nothing else. The _acme-challenge TXT records appear here for a few dozen
; seconds during validation and are removed again by lego.
